        "type": "claim",
        "text": "The hyperechoic appearance of the lesion is more commonly associated with benign breast masses such as simple cysts and lipomas. The lesion's parallel orientation and well-defined circumscribed margins are also indicative of a benign cystic lesion, which aligns with the ACR BI-RADS criteria for a simple breast cyst",
